                <head>225. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On September 26, 1965, Pravda published a report on replies from Shastri and Ayub
                    to Kosygin’s September 17 good offices offer. Shastri expressed appreciation for
                    the offer, but replied that the meeting proposed by Kosygin could only take
                    place after the termination of military actions and the creation of a calmer
                    situation. Ayub also expressed appreciation for Kosygin’s initiative, but took
                    the position that the necessary foundation for the meeting should be prepared
                    through actions taken by the UN Security Council. (Telegram 1032 from Moscow,
                    September 26; National Archives and Records Administration, RG 59, Central Files
                    1964–66, POL 27 INDIA–PAK)</p>
            </div>
